<description>&lt;p&gt;Violent clashes continue between the Viv Ansanm gangs and Haitian security forces, now reinforced by a Kenya-led multinational mission patrolling Port-au-Prince and Kenscoff, while the police high command meets departmental directors. The Dominican army has supplied large ammunition stocks to the 400 Mawozo gang, boosting its firepower, and Taiwan has offered security experience sharing with Haiti. Mayor Jean Massillon of Kenscoff, who warned about gang violence, has died. The European Union provided four million euros for the PMSAN 2 Food Security Program. The UCDP recorded 193 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE1PSDNZYklwbFlURFR4ZWw5TXBzM2kxUUV5SEZfZHFESFdkUVU2Q2tKUHZJSzBNeFNGZmlfTUQtb0pzaFJZNllRRjNMajF1RkJBdkNkcGF4aHVabFF4TzNteUhEQWVsazkxMnhJeFdSZVZfekluWW8xZjJSX2VYQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Trinidad Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilgFBVV95cUxOS1FtSmEtYUR2QjNaUk5aa1BGbHV0OEszYWVMSGFxb1RZS3VnMGxMY2VNQkdNUVNScTlfX3Z6Z091d0stZkdjT1V5U1M0RFdheDRGdndyR21rUHpRdkpBdU1pUzRxTTUtUUp6bmJIMWlXNU9FZ3g1ZFQwdGlhZjNPYUpUeE1NVEgyLW9wa1lwMVIwOTA3d0E?oc=5&quot;&gt;Jamaica Gleaner&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;South Florida Caribbean News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;lenouvelliste.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMickFVX3lxTE8wM0RuNkMxYnczYkN0Y1RtSU9nY2pwWHU0UWo3b3RaZlRVYlhPdUJGZEtsQ1JMS3BNTF9ucG9oZEF3RDJlQ0RRcU1EeWUyVDZEdnhzc0J1ajkxSFp0RTB2TU1NVGJGU1dDMXVncHlKRWFMZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;HaitiLibre.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBM